  "verbalization": "Betamethasone is linked to Renin-angiotensin-aldosterone System-blocker-induced Angioedema through a chain of indications involving Triamcinolone. This relationship is supported by the shared pathway where Betamethasone and Triamcinolone are both indicated for musculoskeletal system disease and miliary tuberculosis, which are distinct but related conditions. The presence of Triamcinolone as a mediator in both pathways suggests a potential role in the pathophysiology of Angioedema, possibly through inflammatory or immunological mechanisms. The evidence highlights a possible overlap in the therapeutic use of these drugs, though the exact mechanism linking Betamethasone to Angioedema remains unclear. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering overlapping indications in drug repurposing studies.",
